  "interpretation": "The earlier apparent precursor or idle-delay effect was confounded by host serial management commands. In two focused production-kernel A/B comparisons, the original RPC client timed out with host log-read commands starting 35 seconds after guest launch and passed when log reads were deferred until 85 seconds, after RPC completion. Network precursors are not necessary for a timeout, and a 26-second idle period alone is not established as causal. Experimental poll-thread scheduling controls were only tested under active host polling and also timed out; they are not production fixes. Each short case is a single boot and does not establish reliability under arbitrary concurrent load."
}
